/**
 * @mainpage UFO Console Module
 * 
 * @section intro Introduction
 * A module for processing console commands with the ability to integrate into embedded systems.
 * Provides a user-friendly interface for creating an interactive command line.
 * 
 * @section features Сapabilities
 * - User command registration (blanks) (blanks)
 * - Automatic parsing of command line arguments
 * - Support for various I/O types (UART, user streams)
 * - Built-in help and exit commands
 * - Move-only design for thread-safe operation
 * 
 * @section architecture Архитектура
 * 
 * The module consists of the following key components:
 * 
 * - **@ref ufo::u_console_t** - main console class (command management)
 * - **@ref ufo::u_console_msg_block_t** - message block (working with input/output in callbacks)
 * - **@ref __u_console::io_base_t** - abstract base class for input/output
 * - **Console-parser** - external module for parsing arguments
 * 
 * @section quick_start Quick start
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "u_cns.h"
 * 
 * // 1. Create an input-output stream (for example, UART)
 * ufo::u_console_uart_stream_t io(&uart_driver);
 * 
 * // 2. Create console
 * ufo::u_console_t console(&io, 255);
 * 
 * // 3. Register commands
 * console.mk_blank("hello", "Prints greeting message", [](const ufo::u_console_msg_block_t& bl) {
 *     bl << "Hello, World!\n";
 * });
 * 
 * // 4. We run it in a separate thread
 * ufo::thread console_task(cns_cfg, &__u_console::console_t::ctask, std::move(cns));
 * console_thread.join();
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section dependencies Dependencies
 * - **Console-parser** - argument parsing module (located in impl/Console-parser/)
 * - **u_sys** - system utilities (streams)
 * - **u_drivers** - device drivers (optional, for UART)
 * 
 * @defgroup public_api Public API
 * @brief Interfaces available to the user for working with the console
 * 
 * @defgroup impl_details Implementation details
 * @brief Inner classes (not intended for direct use)
 * @internal
 */